 ## 2026-07-22
 
+### 0153 — M3 JCS regression now fails closed over its numeric domain (TASK-260715-2kchi0 rework-04)
+- CORRECTION: The jq-equivalent path is now permitted only after source-token validation rejects duplicate keys, negative zero, decimals/exponents, non-finite forms, and integers outside `[-9007199254740991, 9007199254740991]`. A strict independent serializer must emit bytes identical to `jq -cjS` before either row or immutable-manifest hashing proceeds.
+- REGRESSION: Executable controls preserve their exact JSON lexemes and prove schema-valid `installedMemoryBytes=9007199254740993`, `-0`, `1.0`, and `1e3` are rejected before hashing; a symmetric unsafe-negative control also rejects. The positive canonical hash `1872767d…b9abb`, derived run/repetition IDs, immutable hash `221c543f…8fb2`, and one-LF rejection remain unchanged.
+- VERIFICATION: Draft 2020-12 metaschema, five positive and five declared negative compositions, thirteen production-authority hostile mutations, 19 protocol/6 schema/3 PlantUML/1 SVG copies, 12 fixture pairs, both regression copies, semantic rules, 57 task references, privacy/logical-reference/render/board/diff gates, and 332 Swift tests in 29 suites pass. No task, dependency edge, benchmark, tuning winner, or DNS production authority changed.
+
 ### 0134 — Review: current M3 JCS hash is corrected, but the equivalence guard is fail-open (TASK-260715-2kchi0 re-review-03)
